---

## testsmells.org 19-Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10.0 · Class tagged `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Low | 0 | 0 |
| **Total** | **4** | **4** |

4 of 8 test methods are smell-free — a mixed scorecard.

---

### Findings by Severity

---

#### 🔴 HIGH 1 — Sleepy Test (`NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`, line 87)

**Taxonomy:** *Sleepy Test* (testsmells.org)
**Severity rationale:** `Thread.Sleep(3000)` blocks the thread for 3 seconds unconditionally. Even in integration tests, a hard sleep is a smell — it makes the suite slow and introduces timing-dependent failures.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — line 87
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — poll with a timeout instead:**
```csharp
// ✅ Remediated
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(100, cts.Token);   // short poll interval
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** 3 s added to every CI run; if the event is faster or slower than 3 s the test is simultaneously wasteful *and* flaky.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH 2 — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (`BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`, lines 113-119)

**Taxonomy:** *Unknown Test / Empty Test* (testsmells.org)
**Severity rationale:** The method exercises `Insert` 100 times but never asserts anything. MSTest marks it green as long as no exception is thrown, giving false confidence.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion at all
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix — assert the observable outcome:**
```csharp
// ✅ Remediated
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** A silent data-loss bug (e.g., `Insert` silently no-ops after a schema change) would never be caught.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH 3 — Conditional Test Logic (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`, lines 101-108)

**Taxonomy:** *Conditional Test Logic* (testsmells.org)
**Severity rationale:** The `if/else` means only one branch ever executes per run. If the user is always a regular `User`, the `PremiumUser` path is dead code in the test; if it's always `PremiumUser`, the `else` is dead. Either way, the untested branch gives false coverage.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — branching changes which assertion runs
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix — separate into two focused tests:**
```csharp
// ✅ Remediated — one test per scenario
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vera", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** One branch is permanently untested — a bug in the untested path will never surface.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (`InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`, lines 35-38)

**Taxonomy:** *Assertion Roulette* (testsmells.org)
**Severity rationale:** 4 assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the developer must read source to determine *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 bare assertions
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add assertion messages:**
```csharp
// ✅ Remediated
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** CI failure investigation takes longer than it should.

---

### Smells Checked and **Not** Found (Clean)

| Smell | Status | Note |
|-------|--------|------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | In-memory SQLite is a hermetic fixture — appropriate for integration tests |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean | `3` and `10` in count assertions match items just created — self-documenting |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` in any test |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No duplicated assertion statements |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests calling `Insert` use it for setup, not as the action under test |
| Constructor Init | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is descriptive |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.Write*` calls |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB is always available |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | No completely empty test bodies |

### Smell-Free Tests Worth Highlighting

`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are well-structured: clear arrange-act-assert, focused scope, and proper assertions.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Effort | Why First |
|----------|-------|------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | ~2 min | Prevents a false-pass right now |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | ~5 min | One branch is permanently untested |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | ~10 min | Removes 3 s of dead wait + flakiness risk |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | ~2 min | CI ergonomics improvement |

Fixes 1 and 4 are two-minute changes; fix 2 is a straightforward split; fix 3 requires a small polling loop but eliminates the biggest flakiness risk. All four can be done in a single short session.
